Chapter: SheetGraphTest
  cites Sheets chapter CellGraph
  cites Sheets chapter CellStore
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 The order must be DERIVED, and the only way an arm can say so is to
 build a sheet whose derived order differs from both of the orders that
 look right. `A1 = B1 + 1` typed first and `B1 = C1 + 1` typed second
 gives typing order A1 B1 and row-major order A1 B1, and the correct
 order is B1 A1. An arm whose chain runs left to right agrees with all
 three and measures nothing.

 The range line holds the half the parser cannot: `A1:A3` names A2, so a
 formula in A2 must precede a formula summing the range. The parser
 answers only the two corners, and a graph that used them directly would
 put A2 after the sum and still print a plausible order.

 The cycle line holds that a cycle is a REPORT naming the cells rather
 than a spin or a truncated order.

 The edit lines hold the incremental path. Editing a DATA cell is the
 common edit and the cell holds no formula, so the roots of the walk are
 the formulas naming the cell directly; an implementation that only
 handles editing a formula cell answers "(none)" here, which reads as
 "nothing to recompute" and is the worst available wrong answer.

 The independent cell E1 exists as the control: E1 appears in the full
 order and must NOT appear in any dependents answer, so a walk that
 marked everything would fail one line while the others stood.

 The sabotage: return `pl-order` unfiltered from `graph-dependents` and
 the two edit lines gain E1; use the range's corners without expanding
 and the range line loses A2; seed Kahn's queue in row-major order and
 the first line prints A1 B1.

Section: Body

  sg-rows : Integer = 8
  sg-cols : Integer = 8

  sg-sheet : Integer
  sg-sheet = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256

  sg-plan-say : Program -> Text
  sg-plan-say (pg) =
    let p = graph-plan pg
    in if p.pl-ok then graph-order-names pg p
    else "REFUSED: " & p.pl-msg

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let s1 = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256
    in let g1 = graph-put (graph-put (graph-new s1) 0 0 "=B1+1") 0 1 "=C1+1"
    in let s2 = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256
    in let g2 = graph-put (graph-put (graph-new s2) 0 3 "=SUM(A1:A3)") 1 0 "=A1+1"
    in let s3 = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256
    in let g3 = graph-put (graph-put (graph-new s3) 0 0 "=B1+1") 0 1 "=A1+1"
    in let s4 = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256
    in let g4a = graph-put (graph-put (graph-new s4) 0 1 "=A1+1") 0 2 "=B1+1"
    in let g4 = graph-put (graph-put g4a 0 3 "=C1+1") 0 4 "=99"
    in let s5 = sheet-new sg-rows sg-cols 256
    in let g5 = graph-put (graph-new s5) 0 0 "=B1+"
    in act
      print-line-uni ("derived order beats typing and row-major: " & sg-plan-say g1)
      print-line-uni ("a range names the cells between its corners: " & sg-plan-say g2)
      print-line-uni ("a cycle is named, not spun: " & sg-plan-say g3)
      print-line-uni ("the full order of the chain plus an independent cell: " & sg-plan-say g4)
      print-line-uni ("editing the DATA cell A1 recomputes: " & graph-dependent-names g4 0 0)
      print-line-uni ("editing the FORMULA cell C1 recomputes: " & graph-dependent-names g4 0 2)
      print-line-uni ("editing the independent cell E1 recomputes: " & graph-dependent-names g4 0 4)
      print-line-uni ("editing a cell nothing names recomputes: " & graph-dependent-names g4 5 5)
      print-line-uni ("a formula that does not parse is reported before the sort: " & sg-plan-say g5)
      print-line-uni ("a second formula for one cell replaces the first: entries " & show (graph-count (graph-put g5 0 0 "=1+1")))
    end
